this mission to save a five-year-old boy  has gripped morocco for days  rayanne fell into the bottom of the well  while playing outside on tuesday he's  been trapped ever since  the well is in the town of bob beret  it's 32 meters deep but his face is too  narrow for rescue workers to go down and  reach him they've cut a hole into a hill  next to the well hoping they can dig a  horizontal tunnel to get the boy  there  they turned on the light on the phone's  camera and dropped it down so they  discovered that the kid is still there  and he was still talking i heard him  myself he was begging us to save him  the weather is cold and it's unclear  whether the boy has taken any food water  or oxygen that's been channeled to him  i hope he will come out of this okay  it's like one of our own children has  fallen we are praying for his safety  he's one of our children  the hills have turned into a  construction site with hundreds of  people surrounding the area anxiously  waiting for rayanne to be rescued  millions in morocco are watching the  operation unfold live on television on  social media support is also growing  rescue workers say they're getting  closer to the boy but there's a risk of  a landslide  we're living in a true catastrophe in  this area with our son ryan we pray to  god for good news to make us and all  moroccans happy  a helicopter is standing by to take  riyan to hospital and across morocco and  the world people are also waiting and  hoping he'll be saved  taxia lopez obayan al jazeera
 

